3. Product Goal & Problem Statement
Domain & Problem Identification
In small service businesses (e.g., "Scissors & Comb Barbershop" in Kadıköy), appointment booking is handled manually over phone calls or WhatsApp messages. This leads to frequent interruptions during service delivery, accidental double-booking errors, and lost customers due to delayed responses outside operating hours.

Product Goal
To develop a working, simple, and reliable web-based appointment management system where a small business can manage its services and schedule, and customers can view real-time available time slots and book conflict-free appointments within 1 minute without making a phone call.

Target Users
•	Business Owner (Barış Usta): Defines service duration, configures working hours, and views/manages daily calendar appointments.

•	Customer (Caner Sever): Views real-time open slots, books conflict-free appointments, and tracks or cancels existing bookings.

4. Candidate User Journeys
1.	User Journey 1: Customer Conflict-Free Booking

a.	Caner opens the site, selects "Beard Trim & Skin Care (45 Min)".

b.	The system checks the schedule and presents only unreserved 45-minute slots.

c.	Caner picks Tuesday at 14:00, enters his contact details, and clicks "Confirm Appointment".

d.	The system locks the slot and presents a booking confirmation code.

2.	User Journey 2: Owner Schedule & Status Management

a.	Barış Usta logs into the admin panel to view the hourly schedule for the day.

b.	After completing Caner's service, Barış marks the appointment as "Completed".

c.	If a client misses their appointment, Barış marks it as "No-Show/Cancelled", which instantly frees up that time slot on the public calendar.

3.	User Journey 3: Customer Lookup & Self-Cancellation

a.	Caner needs to reschedule due to an emergency, so he accesses the booking lookup page using his phone number.

b.	He locates his upcoming reservation and clicks "Cancel Appointment" (allowed up to 2 hours prior to the slot time).

5. Assumptions & Out-of-Scope List
Key Assumptions
•	Customers have web access on modern desktop or mobile browsers.

•	Time slots are temporarily locked for 5 minutes during active booking selection to prevent race conditions between simultaneous users.

•	The system serves a single business unit operating at one location.

Explicit Out-of-Scope List
•	 Online Credit Card / Payment Gateways: Payments are strictly handled in-person at the shop.

•	 Third-Party Paid SMS / WhatsApp APIs: Confirmation notices are displayed on-screen and simulated via email.

•	 Native Mobile Applications (iOS/Android): The application will be a fully responsive web app only.

•	 Multi-Tenant / Multi-Branch Infrastructure: Initial scope supports only one business entity and one unified calendar.

